  "description": "The proposal involves the installation of two NIBE F2050 10kW air source heat pump (ASHP) units at the front of the property at 98 Highbury Hill, London, N5 1AT — a two-storey family dwelling with a lower ground level.\n\nThe ASHP units will be installed within a recessed area adjacent to the front elevation, at ground level, and screened by existing boundary walls and planting. This discreet location ensures the units are not visible from the public realm and do not negatively impact the character or appearance of the building or the surrounding streetscape.\n\nThe ASHPs will replace the existing gas heating system and serve both space and domestic hot water heating needs for the property. The system will operate at high efficiency and low noise output, with technical specifications confirming compliance with relevant acoustic thresholds as set out by Islington Council.\n\nThe proposal forms part of a wider sustainability-led refurbishment of the home, which also includes internal insulation, replacement of existing windows with high-performance double glazing, and installation of rooftop solar photovoltaic (PV) panels.",
